The optional English word segmentation data and algorithm are adapted from
OpenEVV commit 103277c72b4b1a4dc4c5a91fb9d0ddf0d75f87db, under the MIT
license in OpenEVV-wordseg-LICENSE.txt. https://github.com/Mudb0y/openevv

OpenEVV's sayable and pieces tables were generated from the Moby word lists,
which Grady Ward placed in the public domain, and from the 1993 Carnegie
Mellon Pronouncing Dictionary, copyright 1993 Carnegie Mellon University,
whose use for any research or commercial purpose is unrestricted with
acknowledgement. OpenEVV's tables also include its language data and manually
curated technical words. Their original comments are retained in the files.

Reference-checked English compound readings also use CMUdict revision
74790861f652b15e4ac49015a90074ad62a27690; its full license is in the
project's ReLoq-C-NOTICE.txt (NOTICE in the source tree).
British reference checks also use the GPL-3.0 en_UK dataset from ipa-dict,
based on Leo Boiko's ipacards; see ReLoq-C-NOTICE.txt for attribution.
